    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d575">

                <pb facs="0733" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.65/659: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-16T18:00:00+01:00">November 16, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 16—3 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>337. Embassy’s 322, November 5, noon.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d575-f1"/> It is
                    officially announced that the British Ambassador was received by Count Ciano
                    this morning and informed him that the British Government had decided to
                    recognize Italian sovereignty over Ethiopia. At the same time Perth presented
                    new letters accrediting him to the King of Italy Emperor of Ethiopia.</p>
                <p>This afternoon Ciano and Perth signed a joint declaration<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d575-f2"/> putting into effect the Anglo-Italian accord signed on
                    April 16 and took steps to inform the Egyptian Government.</p>
                <p>Although the newspapers welcome today’s events as restoring the possibility of
                    new and frank collaboration between the two “empires” emphasis is primarily laid
                    upon the recognition by Great Britain of the Empire. The <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tribuna</hi> adds that in fact the restoration of relations between the two
                    countries took place 7 months ago and that the intervening period has served to
                    create a new atmosphere in which the accord may operate and produce useful
                    results.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
